So, here is the story (standard fare, I suppose, apart from the stupid 
bits...)

Fairly ordinary start. Int 20, which was nice, force-bolt and detect 
monsters, IIRC. Nothing special in rings (protection from 
shapechangers). No magic-marker.

Set out, as I usually do with towards Sokoban as I had died to often 
when I first tried out Nethack. Pet died pretty fast on the way. Had to 
force-bolt one boulder in Sokoban, when a monster got trapped behind.
A close call at the zoo, got an amulet of reflection (I had hoped for
a bag of holding).

One my way back to the Mines I found a wand of wishing! So I got myself
2 blessed scrolls of charging (got only one used that on the wand)
a blessed+2 silver dragon scale mail
blessed bag of holding
blessed +2 rustproof Magicbane

I got lucky again, when I found an amulet of life-saving in the mines.
I should point out that I had played this game on my Zaurus PDA, which 
didn`t display a status line. So I had to switch forwards and backwards 
constantly to check on health and current status. Pretty annoying and 
tedious. Anyway that was how I blew my first amulet, with YASD of 
fainting-in-the-presence-of-monsters.

Even before I arrived in minetown I met a mindflayer (first encounter 
ever). I blew the last wish of my wand on a blessed scroll of genocide 
(wished for 2 again, got only one). In any case, it was my first ever 
genocide, and since I had wished for a blessed scroll I suddenly 
realised that I had to wipe out dwarves and hobbits along with the 
mindflayers. Oh well, I do not like their taste, anyway.

Cross-aligned temple in minetown. I NEVER have enough money to buy 
protection (was around level 9, then). Nothing special in the shops. 
Didn't have a pet, but I couldn't resist going into the bookshop. Wanted 
to find out, what would happen, so just read one book. Shopkeeper wanted 
to charge me. I happily paid, since it was a spellbook of identify!

One my way down to mines-end I found two bone-piles, one with a cursed 
+3 small shield. Poor Valkyrie. Got the gems and luckstone from the 
winecellar and back to minetown. Sold two identified diamonds and bought 
protection twice. I seem to have lost it again, because after two more 
donations I still had naked AC of 8. I have no clue, how that happened, 
will have to look it up.

On to the quest for the first time (I had never before finished both 
mines _and_ Sokoban with the same character). Although I zapped and 
killed one helper of the quest-giver by accident I could still start the 
quest. That is, I could have, if I had been level 14.

Down the dungeon I found an altar, converted it, enjoyed myself with 
"create monster". Got +0 Orcrist for that. Not exactly exciting, but, 
hey, at least I can use swords now, apparently. One of the monsters I 
created was big and red and turned out to be an incubus. Nice. Never saw 
one before, so read the spoilers (I confess), checked int and cha (20 
and 10, respectively) and got myself lots of energy and levels (lvl 19), 
since a second incubus joined in at some time.

Returned to the quest. The Dark One immediately spawned a jabberwock and 
teleported away when I hit him. Jabberwock sounded dangerous, so I left 
the room and closed and locked it. Some more fighting, some more created 
monsters, some more door-locking, some more teleportation. Most of the 
time he hopped to the stairs and went up and I used all of my teleport 
scrolls to get him. I know now, that I should have teleported there 
first, and blocked the stairs.
Anyway, he finally went down, right in the tower of the quest-giver, of 
course not before creating another set of monsters.

When I took down the created monsters I commited the first stupidity: I 
don't remember why, but I must have taken of Magicbane and some point. 
But it only realised I had been fighting the dragons and whatnot 
bare-handed when I left the quest-levels. Should have taught me to read 
those game-messages, but I was to learn that the hard way. More on that 
later.

So, did the preparations. Set up an item-stash (Elbereth under chest 
under amulet of strangulation, just in case). Dug broad tunnels between 
all the stairs (that idea I got from reading Maniacs ascension guide).

Down again. Found a magic marker, wrote myself a spell-book of 
agic-missile (my first time ever application of a marker)
and some scrolls of enchant armor (first time ever enchanting of armor)
In order to stop these "First time" side-remarks: It was all first-time 
from now on: I had never before done anything besides force-bolting, 
fighting, eating and dying. Never bought protection before, never 
created holy water before, never used a scroll of teleport (I _did_ get 
teleportitis before by eating nymphes or leprechauns, and boy, did I 
find it annoying), never polymorphed anything, never ...).

Speaking of polymorphing, during one visit of the main stash I zapped a 
few stacks of useless stuff, but I only got worse, I only managed to 
create golems and junk. Decided I don't like it. Will try to do without 
next time.

Anyway, with enchantments and cursed destroy armor I got:
blessed fireproof +5 cloak magic resistance
blessed +4 silver dragon scale mail
blessed +2 fireproof gloves of dexterity
blessed +3 small shield

I still wanted to have a helm of brillance (I had no helm whatsoever, at 
that point) and to exchange my high-boots against speed boots or at 
least boots of levitation.

Furthermore I had:
blessed bag of holding,
10 holy water,
blessed luckstone,
blessed +0 unicorn horn,
lots of wands,
lots of rings (unfortunately without my personal favorite, slow digestion),
lots of scrolls,
lots of potions,
and not nearly enough spellbooks for my liking (had healing, sleep, 
clairvoyance, self-written missiles, identify, create/detect monster, 
light).

I was fire-,cold-,poison-,shock-,sleep- resistant. I had teleportitis 
and teleportation control, I was invisible, could see invisible and I 
was fast.
Afterwards I managed to loose teleportitis again, I don't know how, I 
firmly believe that a gremlin which I had managed to upset
stole it from me.

So, I was pretty happy with myself and imagined that ascension was just 
a few steps away.

Now for more stupidities. To say it in advance, I managed to destroy my 
most valuable possessions twice. The first time it occured, when I 
stumbled into medusas level. I had read something about a titan being on 
medusas level, so when I heard one casting a spell (having taken two 
steps into the level) I though that I had arrived right in medusas lair 
and immediately put on my towel. There and then, I should have looked 
around the map to see that medusa actually wasn't in the room with me 
and taken of my towel again. Stupid me.
Anyway, from the distribution of monsters (lots of such summoned by the 
titans inside the first room, water monsters outside) I concluded that I 
was in a safe room and went around fighting the monster, blindfolded. In 
this way I stumbled into the southernmost of the three water-squares in 
the southeast of the room. Didn't think it mattered, since I _was_ 
wearing an amulet of magical breathing and _had_ greased my back of 
holding, so I thought I'd be fine and tried to get out of the water on 
the  northernmost square.
But grease may wear off apparently, because when I emerged from the pool 
and had finished the fight, I realised I had lost ALL of my scrolls 
(safe one or two scrolls of identify and teleport) and all of my potions 
(had one of confusion left, IIRC).
All hope left me there and then. I didn't believe I could still win the 
game, without my scrolls and my potions, and, worst of all, without my 
spell-books. In this way, quite a few of the castle-wishes were spent 
trying on scrolls of charging to get my books back. The last went into a 
T-shirt and a helm of brillance.


Went down to the graveyard and into the endless mazes of Gehennom (I 
previously thought that there were maybe five or six levels of Gehennom, 
I never expected to have to  get down to level 49!).

The rest consisted of endless digging, exploring and 
going-back-to-stashes to unload stuff. I was especially paranoid about 
food since I had heard something about the amulet burning up those 
rations pretty fast.
Horded wands of digging, too.
Anyhow, after fighting one of the demons, I don't remember which one, I 
went back up towards my stash. When I arrived in Juiblex lair, I put on 
the ring of levitation and set out across the water. Only I didn't.
I had forgotten that I had put on a ring of conflict in addition to the
ring of slow digestion and so couldn't put another one on. As I've 
mentioned: I learned to read those messages the HARD way.
As was to be feared, most scrolls, many potions and all the spell-books 
  (identify and magic-missile, unfortunately) I had with me were lost. 
Again! Although I had been in the water for just one turn! I still can't 
believe it. But, at least, this time around I had left some of the other 
spell-books in my main-stash. I never got another book of 
identification, though.
Anyway, returning to the stash I looked at the charges of my markers and 
decided I could afford another book of magic missile. Along with it I 
wrote two scrolls of gold-detection, which I deemed enough, since I had 
an orb with three charges in my main-stash.

This time, I managed to get down to  Vlad's place before I had the next 
stupid idea. I went up and killed him quite dead. Two magic missile 
including the reflections and he was gone. So, I decided I was 
invincible: I was resistant to everything, had more than 180 HP, 500+ 
energy and an AC of almost -40. So, what could possible go wrong? 
Additionally, I got books magic-mapping spell and levitation and 
invisibilit from the chests. Cool, I thought, let's try out levitation, 
at once. A quick look to the qualifications page revealed I had not 
leveled escape spells yet.
So I zapped the spell happily quite often ( With over 500, I deemed I 
had lots of energy to spare). And _then_ I realised I was in the top of 
a rather small tower with no way to reach the ladder. I ASSUMED, that 
the spell would wear off, otherwise I would be a rather useless spell.
But I, in my folly, had cast the spell several times. What would happen 
if it was accumulative?
I had a lot  of food with me, but still I feared it might not be enough 
and I would die underneath the ceiling of the vampire tower. Quite an 
unique stupid death, I assume.
I thought about zapping cancellation on myself but didn't dare. It 
didn't (and don't) know nearly enough about cancellation and it might 
kill the enchantments of my armor. Or my intrinsics. So I didn't. 
Besides, I realised, the cancellation spell was beyond it's expiration 
date and the respective spell-book had been very effectively cancelled 
by the waters of Medusas lair. Neither did I posess scroll or wand of 
cancellation, as it turned out. So, there was nothing else to do, but 
wait. I killed the remaining vampires and quite a lot of random nasties 
showing up now and again to ease my boredom. When I finally landed I 
launched, dizzy with joy, right into the next stupidity.
I should mention, that I had worn an amulet of magic breathing for 
almost my entire career, and had switched to the amulet of life-saving 
just recently. Therefore, I had become so accustomed to the "Stop 
eating? y/n" message that I was astonished to read "You die. But wait 
..." instead. There went the second amulet of live-saving. It never even 
left Vlads tower, I never found another one, and in the end I ascended 
with my trusty amulet of breathing...

Anyway, I headed down the dungeon, taking the fast-forward approach of 
digging >, become increasingly alarmed and despairing to see an end to 
this accursed Gehennom. When I finally hit rock-bottom, I got out my 
"very rusty corroded dwarvish mattock" and went back to my favourite 
pastime, building a highway through hell.

Went up once more to spend my hard-earned gold on some priest to get the 
AC down to -43. Started the long way down with wild determination to get 
out of this dungeon AS SOON AS POSSIBLE.
<Cough>
Well.
<Cough>
I spent QUITE a lot of time searching and zapping of wands of 
secret-door-detection and trying to teleport before I realised that the 
walls of the tower of the wizard were diggable ...
Clearing the zoo was fun, I just fired volleys of magic missile into the 
room. I was a bit annoyed, however, to hear some gelatinuous cubes 
munching away on MY spoils of war (I didn't know they could eat stuff), 
and tried to put an end to that first.
I prepeared for the battle with Rodney by firing missile diagonally 
through the created entrance to kill his minions, froze the moat (I 
_hate_ water) and then primed my wand of death.
Zap.  The ray of death misses the wizard of Yendor. "Double Trouble". 
Zap, dead wizard, wait, there he is again? Zap. It thus took me three 
zaps of wand of death to kill him. I had had two wands, with a total of 
eight charges before the fight, and hated to waste them on the wizard.
Went down to the last level, candle, bell, book, down, missiles into the 
graveyard, run towards tempel, wade through the fire-traps, find the 
door, find a high-priest inside. _And_ the wizard, again. Two more zaps 
of the WoD and there was the amulet!

Grabbed it, and started the long way up. On foot. I never had any unholy 
water (I still don't even know how to make it) and most of my potions 
had found nirvana in the waters of Juiblex's and Medusas lairs anyway, 
so no cursed gain level for me.

Up an up. Found another wand of death, recharged all of them,
zapped another wizard, grabbed all food, wands of digging and gems I 
found in my stashes and left the dungeon for the planes of earth.
I realised quite fast, that I wouldn't need the ten wands of digging.
I realised even faster, that the elementals on the planes are apparently 
somewhat tougher than their wimpy brethren in the dungeon.
But the very first thought upon entering the planes was: Boy, I would 
have been nice to have brought the orb.

Luckily, the marker had just enough charges left for another two scrolls 
of gold-detection and putting on the ring of conflict I crossed
the planes in a hurry. On the plane of water I finally got rid of the 
wands of digging and of eleven of the standard food-rations (I still had 
around 10 K- and C-rations each, I believe, as well as 17 lumps of
royal gelee (I mentioned paranoia, didn't I?)).

Anyway, to cut the story short, I arrived on the astral plane and in my 
joy fired the first magic missile on my guardian angel, instead of on 
the demi-lich (sorry about that) and decided to go left first, where 
famine waited in front of the temple.
So, a quick zap of the wand of death and a run towards the temple!
I entered, it seemed to be the right one, at least there was some 
high-priest of Anhur, but there were also some many other people around, 
I was in a hurry and anyway, I fired a magic missile. It killed things 
and hit the high priest. Subsequently, the high-priest got angry and 
decided to stand right on the altar. By then I had identified the altar 
as the right one and was in no mood to wait till he would be so
kind to step down from the altar, so I just zapped the high-priest with 
my the WoD. Anhur apparently did not get the joke and tried to 
desintegrate me. That was the last straw. I remembered "The Ascension of 
the Ordinary Valkyrie" and I understood it now. I nearly turned back. 
Maybe I should have. Never liked that Anhur-guy at any rate.
Could have tried to convert myself to another alignment, although I 
don't know how to do that. I _had_ stopped to pray to Anhur a long time 
ago. Before I even entered the castle, I believe. I never got crowned.
But in the end I gave him his amulet, got the demigoddesshood and the 
kitsch-choir (btw, I have "see invisible" I should be able see them, 
unless it's just one of these very clever Dolby-surround setups, which
I doubt even Anhur could afford, even if he showed any interest in that 
kind of stuff, which seems unlikely when considering some of the truly 
gruesome offerings he was mighty pleased to receive from me back down in 
the dungeons.)
Then, again, maybe he DID look out for me. Reading through this account 
of my ascension it seems I got more than my fair share of luck. One of 
the bathes could have been desastrous. I still don't know why all the 
purple worms just spat me out again instead of digesting me. I never got 
unexpected surprise visits when fooling around with incubi. Nobody hit 
me with a cockatrice. I didn't get slimed. I got LOTS of wishes. I found 
the right temple on the first try. I ...
Whatever.
I ascended.

Lhara, female elven wizard. Demigoddess.


